  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening women&apos;s networks movement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of this project is to improve African Women&apos;s Development and Communication Network&apos;s (FEMNET&apos;s) capabilities to strengthen their membership ties so as to work closely with them to inform, mobilize and connect African women and girls for realization of gender equality and women&apos;s empowerment. FEMNET is a pan -African umbrella organization aiming to strengthen the role and contribution of African Non Governmental Organisations (NGOs) and individual activists focusing on women&apos;s rights, gender equality and women&apos;s empowerment. As a network, FEMNET facilitates the sharing of information, experiences, ideas and strategies among African women&apos;s NGOs and individual activists as a strategy for strengthening women&apos;s capacity to participate effectively in the development processes at different levels in Africa  Through this project, interventions will: i. Build the capacities of members in policy advocacy and influencing in order to hold their governments accountable to gender equality and women&apos;s rights commitments using existing frameworks including the Maputo Protocol, Beijing Platform for Action and the Post -2015 Development Framework. ii. Create and manage platforms for members to share information, ideas, strategies and experiences for networking, cross -learning, enhancing collaboration and complementarity iii. Strengthen the effective functioning and operation of FEMNET&apos;s Secretariat.  The following five results will be achieved: 1. FEMNET is able to mobilise, coordinate and carry out joint policy and advocacy with its members from different African countries. 2. FEMNET members have the capacity to effectively influence policies on women&apos;s rights and gender equality in their respective countries 3. FEMNET members use emerging Information Communication Technologies (ICTs) to tell their stories and contribute to the body of knowledge on women&apos;s rights and gender equality in Africa and globally 4. African women know about their rights and gender equality</narrative>
  </description>
